    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 8/9: A SMALL COMPLETE GAME - pickups, score, health\nThree classes cooperate only through events, never through references:\n  AdvPlayerStats (on the player): health, score, win and lose.\n  AdvPickup (on every coin/medkit): on overlap it SENDS `AdvPlayerStats.add_score` or `.heal`\n     to whoever touched it, then removes itself.\n  AdvHazard (spikes): on overlap it applies engine damage; AdvPlayerStats listens to the engine's Damage event.\nCompile order: a class that sends another class's event needs that class compiled first (the Send node\nreads the other class's compiled events), so Compile All builds AdvPlayerStats before AdvPickup.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -360
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          260
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. HURT - on overlap call `game::apply_damage(target, amount)`. The ENGINE then raises the `Damage` event on\nthe target, so ANY class (the player's AdvPlayerStats, the AdvStateMachine enemy) can react with\n`On Damage` without knowing hazards exist. The hazard also counts its hits. Prefer the engine event over a\ncustom one whenever the event is generic.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          -70
        ],
        "size": [
          1340,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.8,
          0.3,
          0.3,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "ov",
          "ov_hit",
          "ov_g",
          "ov_add",
          "ov_set"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. WHY NO SCORE LOGIC HERE - the hazard does not know about players, health or the game rules. It only\nreports `damage happened`. Whoever cares (player, enemy, destructible crate) decides what that means.\nKeep reusable world objects dumb and put rules in the objects that own the state.",
        "position": [
          140,
          -10
        ],
        "size": [
          660,
          590
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "ov_g"
        ]
      }
    ],
